  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "Unreal's OWN material-input vocabulary: the names the engine gives the inputs of a material (MP_BaseColor, MP_Normal, MP_EmissiveColor, ...), which is what a studio's texture parameters are named after when they feed them directly. Engine-wide, so it is filed with the engine module and not with any title. A title that names its parameters otherwise states those in its own user layer -- the panel's Unmapped Textures list is where that is said, and it is filed under the PRODUCT.",
